Stdout and stderr
=================

$ echo 'version: 1.2.3'; echo 'warning: 42' >&2; exit 7
|~version: [0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
@~warning: [0-9]+
? 7

Mixed literal and regex assertions
==================================

$ printf 'start\n1.2.3\nend\n'; printf 'warning: 42\ndone\n' >&2
| start
|~[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
| end
@~warning: [0-9]+
@ done

Alternation applies to the whole line
=====================================

$ printf 'foo\nbar\nfoobar\n'
|~foo|bar
|~foo|bar
|~foo|foobar

Whitespace is significant
==========================

$ printf ' 42 \n'
|~ [0-9]+[ ]

Empty patterns and empty output lines
=====================================

$ printf '\n\n'; printf '\n' >&2
|~
|~.*
@~

Literal metacharacters and markers
==================================

$ printf '~literal\n*literal\n[0-9]+\n01\n'; printf '~literal\n' >&2
| ~literal
| *literal
| [0-9]+
| 01
@ ~literal

Backslashes and explicitly requested substring matching
=======================================================

$ printf 'a\\b\nprefix connection refused suffix\n'
|~a\\b
|~.*connection refused.*

Explicit anchors and character classes
======================================

$ printf 'ABC42\n'
|~^[[:upper:]]+[[:digit:]]+$

One arbitrary line
==================

$ echo anything
|~.*

Output without a trailing newline
==================================

$ printf '1.2.3'
|~[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
